# Heat capacity (5 to 350 K) and recommended thermodynamic properties of barium uranate (BaUO4) to 1100 K☆
...
Adiabatic calorimetry was used to determine the low-temperature heat capacity of BaUO4 from 5 to 350 K. No anomalous behavior was observed, the curve of heat capacity against temperature being of the normal sigmoid shape. From these measurements, the following thermodynamic properties (298.15 K) were obtained: Cpo = (125.27±0.25) J K−1 mol−1; So = (153.97 ± 0.31) J K−1 mol−1; {Ho(T) − Ho(0)} = (23291 ± 47) J mol−1;
